// std.Build.Executable is what a recipe declares an output with, and
// outside one there is no build for it to be added to.  The
// interpreter allows the type to be written and ngplc does not, which
// is the direction the subset rule permits.
@start
@impure
fn main():
    _ ← std.Build.Executable{name: "a", root_source_file: "a.ngpl"}
